      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "cv2.seamlessClone (Poisson blending)\n\nInserts the source patch into the destination with seamless color matching - the raw cv2 wrapper, IMAGE links straight in and the blend comes back as an IMAGE. The source is a crop of birds on plain overcast sky, so the whole-rectangle border is uniform sky and Poisson blending drops the flock into the destination sky with NO mask connected (an unconnected mask = clone the entire patch) - only the birds survive, the sky border melts in. p_x/p_y = 600/363 place the patch center in the destination's sky band; the masked region must fit inside the destination at that point. For a source that is NOT on a uniform background, connect a mask sized like the SOURCE patch (white = clone). \n\nTry flags = NORMAL_CLONE for a plain insert or MONOCHROME_TRANSFER to transfer structure only."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
