      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "cv2.photo family showcase (extends the seamlessClone demo above)\n\nTOP - the SAME source patch cloned into the SAME destination three ways (mask left unconnected = clone the whole rectangle, so the modes are the only difference): NORMAL_CLONE pastes the patch with its colours matched to the destination; MIXED_CLONE keeps only the strong source GRADIENTS so the birds survive but the plain sky melts in; MONOCHROME_TRANSFER transfers structure as a single channel.\n\nBOTTOM - the local (region) edits from cv2.photo, each a Poisson / gradient-domain solve seeded by a mask. 'CV Color Range' keys a region of the destination (here the bright sky) into a mask; colorChange re-tints that region by per-channel multipliers and illuminationChange relights it (alpha = local contrast, beta = falloff). textureFlattening instead runs over the WHOLE frame, wiping fine texture between the edges its internal Canny keeps."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
